<title>NORWAY: Statoil takes over Conoco's Barents Sea licence.</title>
<headline>Statoil takes over Conoco's Barents Sea licence.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) has taken over Conoco's operatorship in the Barents Sea, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Statoil's holding in production licence 181, covering blocks 7128/6, 7128/9 and 7129/4, has increased by just over 20 percent to 70.83 percent.</p>
<p>Conoco has now pulled out of the Barents Sea, Statoil said.</p>
<p>Elf Petroleum has also raised its share by almost five percent to 14.17 percent. Amoco's interest is unchanged at 15 percent.</p>
<p>Conoco is a unit of DuPont Co. --Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
